 "question": "Regression check of gbrain's OpenClaw install fix (gbrain#9972, GST-2714; HARN-98 issue GST-3427), not a new experiment: the OpenClaw rows of gbrain-install-2026-11 rerun on gbrain v0.60.760.0 (1597b77ac8b7fe82d671cc9c874a916b33152d57, a pre-release installed by tag; releases/latest still serves v0.60.753.0), with the task, the OpenClaw pin, the scorer and both arms unchanged. In #494 (v0.60.734.0), 11 bare OpenClaw runs saved the fact to gbrain but a fresh session never asked gbrain, because the agent registered MCP by hand and skipped `gbrain setup openclaw`; v0.60.760.0's install docs run `gbrain setup openclaw` in the same step as the MCP registration, and `gbrain search` now prints remembered facts. Arm bare: \"install gbrain\". Arm paste: gbrain's README agent paste prompt at that tag, byte-identical to v0.60.734.0's and v0.60.757.0's, which points at master's INSTALL_FOR_AGENTS.md. Both arms end with the task's version line naming the tag. OpenClaw with Opus 5.5 and GPT-6.1 Sol as before, plus GPT-6.2 Sol (R54), 10 runs per arm: 60 runs. particle-1 is not rerun. Scored mechanically with the same scorer (a+b+c strict primary; rules a and c touch OpenClaw, so as-scored, a+c and a+b+c are all reported). No new deviation for OpenClaw. The image carries the Hermes rerun's declared deviation (the /usr/local/bin/hermes link, 2026-11-21), which touches only the Hermes image. The adapters are unchanged, and every trial is checked for an exit 2 at stop from the bash 5.2.21 trap error, as in the Hermes rerun.",
